1
00:00:07,670 --> 00:00:09,410
Man, I sure miss Julie.

2
00:00:09,630 --> 00:00:11,420
Spanish midgets.

3
00:00:12,090 --> 00:00:14,750
Spanish midgets wrestling...

4
00:00:15,890 --> 00:00:18,500
Julie. Okay, yes, I see how you got there.

5
00:00:24,730 --> 00:00:27,470
You ever figure out what that thing's for?

6
00:00:27,730 --> 00:00:29,640
No, see, I'm trying this screening thing.

7
00:00:29,860 --> 00:00:33,520
I figure if I always answer the phone, people will think I don't have a life.

8
00:00:33,950 --> 00:00:36,030
My God. Rodrigo never gets pinned.

9
00:00:36,280 --> 00:00:38,900
Here comes the beep. You know what to do.

10
00:00:39,080 --> 00:00:40,940
Hello. I'm looking for Bob.

11
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:42,200
This is Jade.

12
00:00:42,370 --> 00:00:45,860
I don't know if you're still at this number, but I was just thinking about us...

13
00:00:46,040 --> 00:00:50,030
and how great it was, and, well, I know it's been three years...

14
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:52,660
but I was kind of hoping we could hook up again.

15
00:00:52,880 --> 00:00:55,870
You know, I barely had the nerve to make this call...

16
00:00:56,130 --> 00:00:58,300
- so you know what I did?     - What?

17
00:00:58,510 --> 00:01:00,500
I got a little drunk...

18
00:01:00,680 --> 00:01:01,720
and naked.

19
00:01:01,930 --> 00:01:03,220
Bob here.

20
00:01:10,450 --> 00:01:14,980
∮ So no one told you life was gonna be this way ∮

21
00:01:15,520 --> 00:01:19,690
∮ Your job's a joke, you're broke, your love life's D.O.A. ∮

22
00:01:20,600 --> 00:01:24,410
∮ It's like you're always stuck in second gear ∮

23
00:01:24,870 --> 00:01:26,970
∮ When it hasn't been your day, ∮

24
00:01:26,970 --> 00:01:29,970
∮ your week, your month, or even your year ∮

25
00:01:29,970 --> 00:01:33,930
∮ but I'll be there for you ∮

26
00:01:33,930 --> 00:01:35,760
∮ When the rain starts to pour ∮

27
00:01:35,760 --> 00:01:38,880
∮ I'll be there for you ∮

28
00:01:38,880 --> 00:01:40,720
∮ Like I've been there before ∮

29
00:01:40,720 --> 00:01:43,730
∮ I'll be there for you ∮

30
00:01:43,730 --> 00:01:47,390
∮ 'Cause you're there for me too ∮

31
00:01:51,900 --> 00:01:54,730
So, uh, what have you been up to?

32
00:01:54,940 --> 00:01:56,600
Oh, you know, the usual.

33
00:01:56,860 --> 00:01:58,150
Teaching aerobics...

34
00:01:59,070 --> 00:02:01,190
partying way too much. Heh.

35
00:02:01,580 --> 00:02:03,280
Oh, and in case you were wondering...

36
00:02:03,540 --> 00:02:07,450
those are my legs on the new James Bond poster.

37
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,870
Can you hold on a moment? I have another call.

38
00:02:13,090 --> 00:02:14,750
- I love her.     - I know.

39
00:02:17,050 --> 00:02:19,130
- I'm back.     - So are we gonna get together?

40
00:02:19,340 --> 00:02:20,750
Uh, absolutely.

41
00:02:20,930 --> 00:02:22,630
Uh, how about tomorrow afternoon?

42
00:02:22,850 --> 00:02:25,550
Do you know, uh, Central Perk in the village? Say, five-ish?

43
00:02:25,770 --> 00:02:28,630
- Great. I'll see you then.     - Okay.

44
00:02:30,270 --> 00:02:31,760
Okay.

45
00:02:32,310 --> 00:02:34,520
Having a phone has finally paid off.

46
00:02:36,820 --> 00:02:39,100
Even though you do do a good Bob impression...

47
00:02:39,280 --> 00:02:41,320
I'm thinking when she sees you tomorrow...

48
00:02:41,490 --> 00:02:43,610
she's probably gonna realize, hey, you're not Bob.

49
00:02:45,290 --> 00:02:47,280
I am hoping that when Bob doesn't show up...

50
00:02:47,450 --> 00:02:52,320
she will seek comfort in the open arms of the wry stranger at the next table.

51
00:02:52,540 --> 00:02:55,280
Oh, my God. You are pure evil.

52
00:02:56,630 --> 00:02:58,170
Okay, pure evil...

53
00:02:59,050 --> 00:03:00,630
horny and alone.

54
00:03:03,640 --> 00:03:05,050
I've done this.

55
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:13,350
Yeah, yeah, everybody's here.

56
00:03:14,360 --> 00:03:16,810
Hey, everybody. Say hi to Julie in New Mexico.

57
00:03:16,980 --> 00:03:18,020
Hi, Julie.

58
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:19,770
Hi, Julie.

59
00:03:21,610 --> 00:03:23,230
Okay. While Ross is on the phone...

60
00:03:23,410 --> 00:03:25,940
everybody owes me 62 bucks for his birthday.

61
00:03:26,120 --> 00:03:30,280
Um, is there any chance that you're rounding up from...

62
00:03:32,170 --> 00:03:34,830
you know, from like 20?

63
00:03:35,880 --> 00:03:38,790
Hey, come on, we got the gift, the concert and the cake.

64
00:03:39,010 --> 00:03:40,710
Do we need a cake?

65
00:03:42,300 --> 00:03:43,840
Look, I know it's a little steep.

66
00:03:44,390 --> 00:03:45,510
Whoosh.

67
00:03:47,100 --> 00:03:48,590
But it's Ross.

68
00:03:50,060 --> 00:03:52,220
- Yeah, it's Ross.     - Yeah, you're right.

69
00:03:52,390 --> 00:03:54,680
All right? Okay. I'll see you later. I gotta go...

70
00:03:54,940 --> 00:03:56,550
do a thing.

71
00:03:57,610 --> 00:03:59,720
Okay, sweetheart, I'll call you later tonight.

72
00:03:59,900 --> 00:04:02,890
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Hey, you're not really going through with this, are you?

73
00:04:03,280 --> 00:04:05,520
You know, I think I might just.

74
00:04:07,950 --> 00:04:10,690
So, uh, what are you guys doing for dinner tonight?

75
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:14,960
Well, I guess I gotta start saving up for Ross' birthday.

76
00:04:15,920 --> 00:04:18,830
So I guess I'll just stay home and eat dust bunnies.

77
00:04:19,130 --> 00:04:21,460
Can you believe how much this is gonna cost?

78
00:04:22,010 --> 00:04:24,920
Do you guys ever get the feeling that, um...

79
00:04:25,180 --> 00:04:26,540
Chandler and those guys...

80
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:29,930
just don't get that we don't make as much money as they do?

81
00:04:30,140 --> 00:04:31,300
- Yes.     - Really?

82
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:34,470
It's like they're always saying, "Let's go here, let's go there."

83
00:04:34,640 --> 00:04:37,730
- Like we can afford to go here and there.     - Yeah.

84
00:04:37,900 --> 00:04:42,110
Yes, and we always have to go to, you know, someplace nice, you know?

85
00:04:42,280 --> 00:04:47,070
It's not like we can say anything about it, because, like, this is a birthday thing...

86
00:04:47,240 --> 00:04:48,730
you know, and it's for Ross.

87
00:04:48,950 --> 00:04:50,410
- For Ross.     - For Ross.

88
00:04:53,120 --> 00:04:54,280
Oh, my God.

89
00:04:54,540 --> 00:04:55,620
- Hi.     - What?

90
00:04:55,830 --> 00:04:57,620
Okay. I'm at work...

91
00:04:57,790 --> 00:05:01,000
just an ordinary day, you know, chop, chop, sauté, sauté.

92
00:05:01,880 --> 00:05:04,840
All of a sudden, Leon, the manager, calls me into his office.

93
00:05:05,010 --> 00:05:08,170
Turns out they fired the head lunch chef, and guess who got the job.

94
00:05:08,430 --> 00:05:11,170
If it's not you, this is a horrible story.

95
00:05:12,600 --> 00:05:14,720
- Fortunately, it is me.     - Oh.

96
00:05:14,890 --> 00:05:17,350
And they made me head of purchasing, thank you very much.

97
00:05:17,560 --> 00:05:19,180
That's so cool.

98
00:05:19,690 --> 00:05:22,730
Anyway, I just ran into Chandler and Ross. We should go out and celebrate.

99
00:05:22,900 --> 00:05:24,890
You know, someplace nice.

100
00:05:30,370 --> 00:05:31,860
- Someplace nice.     - Yeah.

101
00:05:32,240 --> 00:05:34,830
How much you think I can get for my kidney?

102
00:05:35,960 --> 00:05:38,740

103
00:05:41,750 --> 00:05:43,370
I'm telling you, you can't do this.

104
00:05:43,550 --> 00:05:47,510
Oh, come on, I can't get a girl like that with conventional methods.

105
00:05:47,760 --> 00:05:48,790
That doesn't matter.

106
00:05:48,970 --> 00:05:50,330
She wanted to call Bob.

107
00:05:50,510 --> 00:05:53,880
Hey, for all we know, Bob is who she was meant to be with.

108
00:05:54,100 --> 00:05:57,010
You may be destroying two people's chance for happiness.

109
00:05:57,230 --> 00:05:58,720
We don't know Bob.

110
00:05:59,770 --> 00:06:03,140
Okay? We know me. We like me. Please let me be happy.

111
00:06:04,530 --> 00:06:07,480
Go over there and tell that woman the truth.

112
00:06:08,610 --> 00:06:09,650
All right.

113
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:12,150
Go.

114
00:06:19,580 --> 00:06:20,660
Hi.

115
00:06:21,170 --> 00:06:22,250
Hi.

116
00:06:23,340 --> 00:06:25,080
Listen, I have to, uh, ahem...

117
00:06:25,260 --> 00:06:27,210
I have to confess something.

118
00:06:27,760 --> 00:06:29,500
Yes?

119
00:06:31,300 --> 00:06:33,720
Whoever stood you up is a jerk.

120
00:06:34,680 --> 00:06:36,760
- How did you...     - I don't know.

121
00:06:38,940 --> 00:06:43,180
I just had this weird sense. You know? But that's me, I'm weird and sensitive.

122
00:06:46,280 --> 00:06:47,360
Tissue?

123
00:06:48,360 --> 00:06:49,400
Thanks.

124
00:06:50,990 --> 00:06:52,730
No, no, you keep the pack.

125
00:06:53,530 --> 00:06:55,070
I'm all cried out today.

126
00:07:08,420 --> 00:07:10,000
Okay, okay.

127
00:07:10,970 --> 00:07:14,380
Here is to my sister, the newly appointed head lunch chef.

128
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:16,550
Who is also in charge of purchasing.

129
00:07:16,770 --> 00:07:19,680
Newly appointed head lunch chef, also in charge of purchasing...

130
00:07:19,940 --> 00:07:23,180
Who has her own little desk when Roland's not there.

131
00:07:23,900 --> 00:07:27,810
Uh, lunch chef, purchasing, own little desk when Roland's not there...

132
00:07:28,030 --> 00:07:31,110
- here's to my little sister...     - Oh, wait. And I got a beeper.

133
00:07:31,360 --> 00:07:32,520
Oh, cool.

134
00:07:34,660 --> 00:07:37,240
- That's fine, I'll just wait.     - Aw, sorry.

135
00:07:37,410 --> 00:07:39,030
Oh, sorry, sorry.

136
00:07:39,660 --> 00:07:40,740
Monica.

137
00:07:43,790 --> 00:07:45,160
Are we ready to order?

138
00:07:45,340 --> 00:07:47,000
Oh. You know, we haven't even looked yet.

139
00:07:47,250 --> 00:07:48,910
Well, when you do, just let me know.

140
00:07:49,090 --> 00:07:51,830
I'll be right over there on the edge of my seat.

141
00:07:57,430 --> 00:07:58,920
Wow, look at these prices.

142
00:07:59,140 --> 00:08:01,760
Yeah, these are pretty "cha-ching."

143
00:08:02,890 --> 00:08:05,760
I know. What are these, famous chickens?

144
00:08:07,150 --> 00:08:09,730
- Sorry I'm late. Congratulations, Mon.     - Thanks.

145
00:08:09,990 --> 00:08:13,070
I'm not sorry I'm late. How incredible was my afternoon with Jade?

146
00:08:13,240 --> 00:08:17,650
Well, pretty incredible, according to the message she left on my machine.

147
00:08:18,410 --> 00:08:22,570
Hey, Chandler, why is this woman leaving a message for you on my machine?

148
00:08:22,750 --> 00:08:24,990
See, I had to tell her that my number was your number.

149
00:08:25,170 --> 00:08:27,280
I couldn't tell her my number was my number...

150
00:08:27,460 --> 00:08:30,120
because she thinks my number is Bob's number.

151
00:08:31,420 --> 00:08:34,920
Hey, tell me again. What do I do when Mr. Roper calls?

152
00:08:36,550 --> 00:08:37,710
Do I dare ask?

153
00:08:37,930 --> 00:08:41,340
Yes, I'll start with the carpaccio, and then I'll have the grilled prawns.

154
00:08:41,560 --> 00:08:44,930
- That sounds great, same for me.     - And for the gentleman?

155
00:08:45,100 --> 00:08:46,930
Yeah, I'll have the Thai chicken pizza.

156
00:08:47,110 --> 00:08:50,190
But, hey, look, if I get it without the nuts and leeks and stuff...

157
00:08:50,360 --> 00:08:52,220
is it cheaper?

158
00:08:52,490 --> 00:08:54,730
You'd think, wouldn't you?

159
00:08:55,280 --> 00:08:57,070
- Miss?     - Okay.

160
00:08:57,320 --> 00:09:00,190
I will have the, uh... side salad.

161
00:09:00,950 --> 00:09:03,070
And what would that be on the side of?

162
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:05,040
I don't know.

163
00:09:05,250 --> 00:09:08,240
Why don't you just put it right here next to my water?

164
00:09:10,960 --> 00:09:12,040
And for you?

165
00:09:12,340 --> 00:09:16,830
Um, I'm gonna have a cup of the cucumber soup...

166
00:09:17,010 --> 00:09:18,550
and, um...

167
00:09:20,430 --> 00:09:21,840
take care.

168
00:09:24,730 --> 00:09:27,890
- I will have the, uh, Cajun catfish.     - Anything else?

169
00:09:28,150 --> 00:09:30,890
Yes, how about a verse of "Killing Me Softly"?

170
00:09:32,980 --> 00:09:35,600
You're gonna sneeze in my fish, aren't you?

171
00:09:41,330 --> 00:09:43,990
Plus tip, divided by six...

172
00:09:45,120 --> 00:09:47,200
Okay, everyone owes 28 bucks.

173
00:09:48,830 --> 00:09:50,240
Um, everyone?

174
00:09:52,050 --> 00:09:53,250
Oh. You're right, I'm sorry.

175
00:09:53,420 --> 00:09:54,460
Thank you.

176
00:09:54,670 --> 00:09:57,130
It's Monica's big night. She shouldn't pay.

177
00:09:57,510 --> 00:09:58,590
Aw, thank you.

178
00:09:58,760 --> 00:10:00,470
So five of us is...

179
00:10:01,510 --> 00:10:03,220
33.50 apiece.

180
00:10:03,430 --> 00:10:05,890
No. Uh-uh. No way. Sorry, not gonna happen.

181
00:10:07,020 --> 00:10:08,970
Whoa. Whoa. Prom night flashback.

182
00:10:11,190 --> 00:10:13,980
Sorry, Monica. I'm really happy you got promoted...

183
00:10:14,190 --> 00:10:17,400
but cold cucumber mush for 30-something bucks?

184
00:10:17,570 --> 00:10:18,610
No.

185
00:10:19,990 --> 00:10:22,530
Rachel just had that little salad...

186
00:10:22,740 --> 00:10:26,080
and Joey with his, like, teeny pizza.

187
00:10:26,620 --> 00:10:28,200
Okay, Pheebs.

188
00:10:28,790 --> 00:10:31,500
How about we'll each just pay for what we had, okay?

189
00:10:31,710 --> 00:10:34,120
- It's no big deal.     - Not for you.

190
00:10:38,630 --> 00:10:40,170
All right, what's going on?

191
00:10:40,930 --> 00:10:43,540
Okay, look, I really don't wanna get into this right now.

192
00:10:43,720 --> 00:10:46,880
- It'll just make everybody uncomfortable.     - Oh, fine. All right, fine.

193
00:10:47,100 --> 00:10:49,220
- What? Whoa, whoa.     - You can tell us.

194
00:10:49,440 --> 00:10:52,270
Yeah, hello? It's us. All right? We'll be fine.

195
00:10:52,440 --> 00:10:53,890
Yeah.

196
00:10:56,780 --> 00:10:58,270
Ahem. Okay, um...

197
00:10:59,950 --> 00:11:03,310
Uh, we three feel like that, uh, ahem...

198
00:11:03,490 --> 00:11:06,900
sometimes you guys don't get that, uh, ahem...

199
00:11:14,540 --> 00:11:16,960
We don't have as much money as you.

200
00:11:20,680 --> 00:11:23,170
- Okay.     - I hear you.

201
00:11:23,930 --> 00:11:25,920
We can talk about that.

202
00:11:26,970 --> 00:11:28,210
Well, then...

203
00:11:29,980 --> 00:11:31,140
let's.

204
00:11:32,730 --> 00:11:38,190
Well, um, I guess I just never think of money as an issue.

205
00:11:38,400 --> 00:11:41,440
- That's because you have it.     - That's a good point.

206
00:11:42,910 --> 00:11:46,650
So, um, how come you guys haven't talked about this before?

207
00:11:46,830 --> 00:11:50,030
Because it's always something, you know? Like with Monica's new job...

208
00:11:50,210 --> 00:11:53,070
or the whole Ross' birthday hoopla.

209
00:11:53,250 --> 00:11:55,210
What? Whoa, hey.

210
00:11:55,380 --> 00:11:59,920
I don't want my birthday to be the source of any kind of negative...

211
00:12:00,130 --> 00:12:02,000
There's gonna be a hoopla?

212
00:12:04,590 --> 00:12:09,090
Basically there's the thing, and then the stuff after the thing and it's...

213
00:12:09,850 --> 00:12:12,810
If it makes anybody feel better, we can just forget the thing...

214
00:12:13,020 --> 00:12:15,060
and we'll just do the gift.

215
00:12:15,270 --> 00:12:17,890
Gift? The thing's not the gift?

216
00:12:18,860 --> 00:12:21,900
No, the thing was we were gonna go see Hootie and the Blowfish.

217
00:12:22,070 --> 00:12:25,860
Hootie and the... Oh, my... I can catch them on the radio.

218
00:12:26,870 --> 00:12:30,030
No. Now I feel bad. You wanna go to the concert.

219
00:12:30,250 --> 00:12:32,660
No, look, hey, it's my birthday...

220
00:12:32,870 --> 00:12:36,040
and the important thing is that we all be together.

221
00:12:36,250 --> 00:12:37,410
- All of us.     - Together.

222
00:12:37,590 --> 00:12:39,200
Not at the concert.

223
00:12:41,130 --> 00:12:43,210
- Okay. Thank you.     - Thanks.

224
00:12:43,380 --> 00:12:44,620
Yeah.

225
00:12:50,640 --> 00:12:53,930
So, the Ebola virus. That's gotta suck, huh?

226
00:12:58,690 --> 00:13:00,560
Gee, Monica. What's in the bag?

227
00:13:00,780 --> 00:13:03,310
I don't know, Chandler. Let's take a look.

228
00:13:03,530 --> 00:13:05,440
Oh, it's like a skit.

229
00:13:07,070 --> 00:13:09,860
Why, it's dinner for six. Five steaks...

230
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:12,410
and an eggplant for Phoebe.

231
00:13:14,540 --> 00:13:18,410
We switched meat suppliers at work, and they gave me the steaks as a thank-you.

232
00:13:18,630 --> 00:13:22,840
But wait, there's more. Hey, Chandler, what is in that envelope?

233
00:13:24,590 --> 00:13:27,080
By the way, this didn't seem so dorky out in the hall.

234
00:13:27,260 --> 00:13:28,340
Come on.

235
00:13:29,100 --> 00:13:32,010
Why, it's six tickets to Hootie and the Blowfish.

236
00:13:35,140 --> 00:13:36,630
The Blowfish.

237
00:13:38,560 --> 00:13:42,270
It's on us, all right? So don't worry. This is our treat.

238
00:13:42,940 --> 00:13:45,020
So... thank you.

239
00:13:48,160 --> 00:13:49,860
Could you be less enthused?

240
00:13:50,070 --> 00:13:52,490
Look, it's a nice gesture. It is.

241
00:13:52,740 --> 00:13:54,480
But it just feels like...

242
00:13:54,950 --> 00:13:55,990
Like?

243
00:13:56,790 --> 00:13:58,950
- Charity.     - Charity?

244
00:13:59,210 --> 00:14:01,540
We're just trying to do a nice thing here.

245
00:14:01,750 --> 00:14:05,840
But, Ross, you have to understand, your nice thing makes us feel about this big.

246
00:14:06,090 --> 00:14:09,000
Actually, it makes us feel that big.

247
00:14:10,180 --> 00:14:14,800
What? I don't understand. I mean, it's like we can't win with you guys.

248
00:14:15,060 --> 00:14:18,140
If you guys feel this big, maybe that's not our fault.

249
00:14:18,390 --> 00:14:20,230
Maybe that's just how you feel.

250
00:14:20,980 --> 00:14:22,400
Oh.

251
00:14:23,150 --> 00:14:28,060
